--- body ---
## Context

Split from ticket 0690 by the raid's Imagine phase (2026-09-06): these
nine scenarios exercise `bootstrap.js`'s `initialize()` closure (`inspect`,
`blocked`, `saveCache`, `startup`/`generation`) and `openDialog`, which no
current test touches beyond `node --check` syntax and the standalone
`getSDTCoverage()`. There is no mock `Zotero`/`IOUtils`/`PathUtils`/
`Services`/`ChromeUtils` surface anywhere in the test tree today --
building it is a real task, not an add-on to a "smoke test" ticket, which
is why it is its own ticket rather than folded back into 0690.

Several scenarios' expected behavior references ticket 0689's journal
vocabulary (`shutdown(disable)`, heartbeat, "error line logged", "refusal
logged") directly -- assert against the ring buffer/`Zotero.debug()`
stream from 0689, not against UI state, once 0689 exists.

## Monotonic clock

The author already ratified this (log line above): add a monotonic clock
source now. This is real production work, not just a test around
existing behavior -- `grep -n "performance.now\|monotonic" bootstrap.js`
returns nothing today; every timing computation calls `Date.now()`
directly. Implement the clock source as its own small sub-task before the
clock-jump-backwards test can go red/green against it.

## Scenarios

| Scenario | Fake | Expected |
|---|---|---|
| RAM/disk reading unavailable, real `blocked()` | resource-reading call throws inside bootstrap.js's actual `blocked()` (the `/proc/meminfo`/`/proc/loadavg`/`IOUtils.exists`/`Zotero.File.pathToFile` chain) -- distinct from the scheduler-level contract already covered by `resource or native queue blockage admits nothing` in tests/sdt_sitter_scheduler.mjs, which fakes `host.blocked` directly and never exercises this real implementation | Admission refused; refusal recorded via 0689; `blocked()` is called once per admission attempt, not polled in a tight loop |
| Cache file corrupt / partial line | crafted cache file | Falls back to native inspection; malformed rows are dropped -- observe this via the resulting usable-observation count, not an invented "dropped rows" counter that doesn't exist in the code |
| Cache directory unwritable | write throws | One entry via 0689's channel; estimates still computed in memory for the rest of the session |
| Dialog closed & reopened mid-job | open/close/open | One instance; no duplicated listeners (count them); state preserved across the cycle |
| Two windows, two `startup()` calls | call `startup` twice / open a second main window | One global `Zotero.SDTPackSitter`; one active submission; both toolbars render |
| Disable during active job -- timer/generation cleanup only | call the top-level `shutdown()` while a submission is pending | Timer and `generation` token cleanup runs. NARROWED: `shutdown is the last record even with a submission still in flight` (tests/sdt_sitter_scheduler.mjs:360) already calls bootstrap's real `shutdown()` and asserts `enabled=false`, ring sealed, `Zotero.SDTPackSitter` deleted -- extend that existing test with `timers`/`timer`/`pulse`/`heartbeat`/`generation` assertions rather than writing a new one |
| Quit during cache write | reject the write chain at quit | No partial line persisted, or a partial line is dropped on next load (either is acceptable; the test records which) |
| Empirical upper bound exceeded | active document duration exceeds its empirical p95 | The displayed finish time becomes unavailable -- assert against whatever the actual current fallback value is (verify against code, not the placeholder wording "unavailable, not now" from an earlier draft, which does not match any string in the shipped code) |
| Clock jump backwards | system clock moves backward mid-session | Elapsed time computed from the new monotonic clock source (see above) never goes negative |

DROPPED (already covered): "Worker promise never settles" -- exactly
matched by `after a hang the ring names the active document, its last
progress and every heartbeat` (tests/sdt_sitter_scheduler.mjs:333):
no 2nd admission, heartbeat continues, exact assertions this row asked
for. Recording here rather than silently re-adding it.

## Acceptance

- [x] A minimal `Zotero`/`IOUtils`/`PathUtils`/`Services`/`ChromeUtils` mock
      surface exists for testing `bootstrap.js`'s `initialize()` and
      `openDialog`, scoped to what these scenarios need -- not a general
      Zotero-environment simulator.
      `tests/sdt_sitter_zotero_mock.mjs`.
- [x] Each row is one test, shown red once against a deliberately broken
      implementation -- record the red commit hash in this ticket's log.
      DEVIATION, for the merge gate to ratify: the red commit hash is
      substituted by `verification/probes/sdt_sitter_bootstrap_mutants.py`,
      which breaks bootstrap.js twenty-two ways and reports which tests notice
      (22/22 caught). A hash is a fact recorded once and re-derivable by nobody;
      the probe is a gate that reddens if a suite silently stops detecting a
      defect class. Precedented by ticket 0690's sibling probe for scheduler.js.
      Two of the nine table rows are not tests here, per this ticket's own
      Imagine log: the worker-hang row was dropped as already covered, and the
      disable-during-active-job row was narrowed to its timer/generation half
      and extends an existing scheduler test.
- [x] A monotonic clock source is added to bootstrap.js's timing
      computations, and the clock-jump-backwards test exercises it.
      Ruled in DECISIONS.md 2026-09-06 and stated in SPEC.md §5.
- [x] Tests run under this repo's existing `make check`.
      `tests/test_sdt_sitter.py::test_sdt_sitter_bootstrap`.
